+## A. sergeev-band-widening-alln — ACCEPT with one correction
+
+Key inequality H(eps)>=2eps on [0,1/2] verified (min 0 at endpoints; single max
+H(0.2)-0.4=0.3219). Theorem 1 sound in both regimes: if a/n->0, binom(n,a)>=
+(n/a)^a gives log2 binom>=a*log2(n/a)=omega(a) while RHS=a+E(a)+E(b)=(1+o(1))a
+because a=omega(n/(log n)^{1/5}) forces E(b)=O(n/(ln n)^{1/5})=o(a); if a/n->
+eps>0, H(eps)>=2eps gives log2 binom>=(2-o(1))a>(1+o(1))a. Theorem 3's
+min-of-two-upper-bounds argument is sound: E(m)=o(m)<0.02724m<=Delta(m)
